=== meta ===
rule: SUBJECT_INPUT_CHANGED
title: New input data beside changed production is refused as repair evidence (D-199)
d199: D-199 (0.12) refuses repair evidence for this rule. The inputs are unchanged; they were the case subject_input_repair_neg, held at warn by that evidence. REPAIR_EVIDENCE_REFUSED pins that the production change still reached the finding.
origin: the rule escalates through repair evidence like every oracle
origin2: rule (SPEC §5 E1) — the production change under the test
origin3: explains the new data, so nothing blocks
=== before: src/app.py ===
def normalize(s):
    return " ".join(s.split())
=== before: tests/test_norm.py ===
from app import normalize


def test_collapse_and_lower():
    assert normalize("  Hello   World  ") == "hello world"
=== after: src/app.py ===
def normalize(s):
    return " ".join(s.split()).lower()
=== after: tests/test_norm.py ===
from app import normalize


def test_collapse_and_lower():
    assert normalize("  hello   world  ") == "hello world"
=== expect ===
